    description: "Phase 3 of ADR-0027, Cluster C. Fold apex/peer overloads to a single canonical per pair: fn → function, var → variable, proc → procedure, structure → struct.\n\nCluster C is the lowest-risk Phase 3 item: consumer-side enumerations don't change (the apex was already in the registry). Producer-side migration replaces the peer label with the apex per the cluster-C audit-findings doc.\n\nFile audit-findings doc at docs/audits/<NN>-symbol-kind-cluster-c-apex-peer-collapse.md per the docs/audits/README.md format spec. Document apex selection per pair (most-frequent-emitter wins, mirroring ADR-0023 heuristic).\n\nAffects ~5-10 producer files (the analyzers emitting peer labels). Tag with awaits_bakeoff_validation at PR merge per BVT discipline.\n\nReference: docs/adr/0027-symbol-kind-language-construct-only.md §\"Phase 3\" and §\"Detailed analysis: per-cluster fold targets\" Cluster C."  # df6b
